On Tue, 25 Mar 2014, Jonathan Ellis wrote:
> It was a white dragon (cold aligned) and the sword was Fire Brand
> (obviously hot aligned). Does the game do extra bonus damage for fire
> against cold, or cold against fire (which would be on top of whatever
> extra fire damage Fire Brand would do to just "any non-fire-resistant
> monster")? Or does the game only recognise resistances, and not
> vulnerabilities?

Until recently I thought so.  But some source diving shows that Nethack is
actually rather inconsistent on this point.  It doesn't apply in the OP's
situation.

Fiery and frosty explosions, such as that caused by the skilled cone of
cold spell and the fireball spell (both skilled and unskilled), do a clean
double damage in this case.

Cold rays do an extra D3 of damage for each D6 they would do normally.
(That's 2D6 normal and 2D3 bonus for a wand.  Dice for breath is set in the
monster tables, and dice for unskilled cone of cold depends on player level.)

Fire rays do a flat 7 points extra damage in this case.

There doesn't seem to be any extra damage for other forms of attack --
including artifact melee.

An additional inconsistency is that extra damage is only applied to NPCs.
This means that an NPC wearing RDSM will take double damage from a frosty
explosion, but the player won't.

